      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T04:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the things I talked with Rupert about yesterday is that we use the dist dir directly instead of doing a post-copy stop so that even if the build dies in the middle, we still get partial artifacts out (most importantly, the log files from soong_ui, but the installed_files.txt and some other ninja-graph generated files have been very useful to debug issues in the past too).\n\nSo I think we need to be pretty careful to keep the log files pointing to the $DIST_DIR directly, and only use the rigged dist dir for the kati/bazel action-graph-generated files. (The log rotating also wouldn\u0027t work properly with the renames)\n\nIf you rebase this, I think this may get somewhat easier, as Patrice just replaced the logic below with config.LogsDir(); so we may be able to get away with having DistDir() be the rigged version when UseBazel() and LogsDir() always be the real one.",
